{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Behold, of the fatness of the earth shall be your dwelling.</b> Since Jacob's eyes are lifted toward the heavens — more than he fixes his eyes upon a land that is naturally fat — therefore concerning Jacob he placed the dew of the heavens before the fatness of the earth, because Jacob's essential trust is in the Holy One, blessed be He, in whose hand are the keys of rain. But the fatness of the earth, which is in human hands to fertilize and to fatten — such trust is to him vain and secondary. But with Esau it is the reverse: he places more trust in his own strength and the might of his hand, by which he can fatten the land, than in lifting his eyes toward the heavens to bring down dew of blessing for him. And because he is among those of little faith, therefore he would choose for his dwelling a land naturally fat; and so the expression ״הִנֵּה מִשְׁמַנֵּי הָאָרֶץ יִהְיֶה מוֹשָׁבֶךָ״ was used — no mention of the giving of Elohim was made concerning him. And ״מוֹשָׁבֶךָ״ ('your dwelling') is mentioned because the implication is that he himself will choose for himself a place of fatness and richness to settle there. But Jacob — he set HaShem as his trust; therefore he is not particular about which land he settles in, for even if it is naturally lean, his heart is confidently relying on HaShem that He will fatten it; and so concerning him it is stated ״וְיִתֶּן לְךָ הָאֱלֹהִים״ ('and may the Elohim give you')." "And some say that he placed the dew first concerning Jacob because, by way of miracle, his land would be fattened by the dew: even if it descends upon a naturally lean land, the dew would fatten it miraculously. But Esau needs to seek out first a fat piece of ground, and only then does the dew help — but in a lean land it does not help. Therefore he must go about to seize a land by his sword; and so immediately after this comes the blessing ״וְעַל חַרְבְּךָ תִחְיֶה״ ('and by your sword you shall live')."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Normalized ה׳ and האלהים to HaShem and Elohim respectively per divine-name rules."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:42.467334892Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}